Construct HostResolverCache::Key with braces.

Key is an aggregate (no constructor). Key(a, b) is C++20's parenthesized aggregate initialization (P0960),
which the clang Westlake builds Cronet with (Chromium's clang 16 from the 109 toolchain) predates; AOSP built
this tree with clang 18. Key{a, b} initializes the same members in the same order, with no narrowing here.

--- a/net/dns/host_resolver_cache.cc
+++ b/net/dns/host_resolver_cache.cc
@@ -369,3 +369,3 @@
   entries_.emplace(
-      Key(std::move(domain_name), network_anonymization_key),
+      Key{std::move(domain_name), network_anonymization_key},
       Entry(std::move(result), source, secure, staleness_generation));
